# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ARES — .gitignore
#
# TWO THINGS THIS FILE CANNOT DO, BOTH OF WHICH HAVE BITTEN US:
#
# 1. It does not untrack anything already tracked. Adding a pattern
#    here has no effect on a file git already knows about — that needs
#    `git rm --cached`. This is why models/*.pt sat in the repo for
#    weeks despite `*.pt` being listed.
#
# 2. Patterns are LITERAL. `.venv/` does not match `.venv-ml/`, which
#    is how a 182 MB push got rejected. Hence `.venv*/` below.
#
# Rule of thumb: run `git status --short && du -sh .git` before a
# commit. If .git grew by more than the diff, something binary slipped
# in.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── macOS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The previous version of this file had `.env -` with a stray trailing
# " -", which is a literal pattern matching a file called ".env -".
# Real .env files were never ignored. CONVENTIONS.md says this repo is
# public and must never carry a credential; that typo was the gap.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Qualcomm AI Hub keeps its token in ~/.qai_hub/client.ini. It lives
# outside the repo, but a copy pasted in here would be a live key in a
# public repository, so it is blocked defensively.
.qai_hub/
client.ini

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv*/
venv*/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Node / frontend ────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── Model weights and exports ──────────────────────────────────────
# Never in git. These go to GitHub Releases — a 54 MB checkpoint in
# history is carried by every clone forever, and the demo does not
# need them: inference is pre-computed into detections.json.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.onnx.orig
*.tflite
*.engine
*.mlmodel
*.bin
*.safetensors
models/

# ...but the two benchmark frames are not models. They are 365 KB of
# JPEG extracted from the demo clip by tools/build_demo_clip.py, and
# the documented benchmark command names one of them directly:
#     python tools/benchmark.py models/yolov12s.pt 960 models/test_frame_dense.jpg
# Keeping them tracked is what makes that command work from a fresh
# clone instead of requiring the clip and a rebuild first.
!models/test_frame.jpg
!models/test_frame_dense.jpg

# ── Training output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
runs/
wandb/
lightning_logs/
*_saved_model/

# ── Datasets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
datasets/
data/raw/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z

# ── Media ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Video is excluded by default, then the one clip the dashboard
# actually plays is added back. Vite serves it at /demo_clip.mp4 and a
# fresh clone cannot run the demo without it, so it is a deliberate
# exception rather than an oversight.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
!frontend/public/demo_clip.mp4

# ── Demo assets that MUST stay tracked ─────────────────────────────
# A clean clone has to run. detections.json is the demo, and the tile
# cache is what makes the map work with the venue wifi down.
!backend/data/detections.json
!backend/data/fixture_detections.json
!backend/data/tiles/
!backend/data/tiles/**

# Alert delivery ledger. RUNTIME STATE, not source: it records which alerts
# actually reached a channel on one machine, so committing it would replay
# another machine's delivery history as this one's — the dashboard would show
# a drained queue it never drained. `backend/alerts.py` recreates it on the
# first flush.
backend/data/alerts.jsonl

# ── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
.claude/

# ── Local working notes ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scratch that documents HOW the work got done rather than what it does.
# Useful while a session is live, noise in a repository someone reads to
# understand the system. Keep them locally if you want them; they do not
# belong in the history.
_to_delete/
SESSION_*.md
*_SESSION.md
NOTES_*.md
scratch/
.DS_Store
